menu "Unit PaHUB Configuration"

    config PAHUB_ADDRESS
        hex "Hub I2C address"
        range 0x70 0x77
        default 0x70
        help
            7-bit address set by the A0-A2 solder straps on the back of the
            unit. The factory setting is 0x70, which clashes with the ENV III
            QMP6988; move one of them if both share Port A.

    config PAHUB_I2C_SPEED_HZ
        int "Hub control-register SCL speed (Hz)"
        range 10000 400000
        default 100000
        help
            Clock for selecting ports. The PCA9548A supports 400 kHz, but the
            selected downstream cable and devices load the bus too, so raise
            it only if the whole Port A tree meets Fast-mode rise times.
            Downstream devices use the speed their own drivers register.

    config PAHUB_DESELECT_WHEN_IDLE
        bool "Turn every port off after each transfer"
        default n
        help
            Leaves the hub with no port selected whenever no transfer or
            unit_pahub_lock() hold is in progress. Enable it when devices
            connected straight to Port A share an address with a device behind
            the hub. Costs one extra control write per transfer.

    config PAHUB_AUTO_RECOVER
        bool "Recover a hung Port A bus automatically"
        default y
        help
            When a hub control write or a downstream transfer times out,
            clock the bus free (releasing a device that holds SDA low) and
            reselect the port on the next access. Control writes are retried
            once after the reset. Disable it only if another I2C master
            shares Port A.

endmenu
